---
// Static page: prerendered at build time (md-mirror parity pipeline
// reads the emitted HTML). Only EmDash CMS routes render on demand.
export const prerender = true;
// Ported verbatim from eagle-ridge-methodology/marketing/path-to-88.html (plan 004).
// Figure numbers are verified claims: do not change any number without rerunning
// them against data/nist-800-171-controls.yaml and the sources in the footer note.
// Copy fixes made here must be back-ported to the methodology repo.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/explainer.css';

const title = 'The Path to 88';
const description = 'What an eight-week CMMC Level 2 engagement does to your SPRS score: from an honest first score below zero to 91, above the 88 conditional-pass line. Representative eight-person machine shop.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/path-to-88">
<div class="explainer">
<div class="wrap">

<section class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">Eagle Ridge Advisory · CMMC Level 2</p>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>The path to 88</h1>
    <p class="dek">Every defense contractor handling CUI is required to have an SPRS score. It runs
    from <strong>110</strong> down to <strong>&minus;203</strong>, and a conditional
    CMMC certification requires at least <strong class="accent">88</strong>.
    Score yourself honestly for the first time and you will probably land far
    below it&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;often below zero.</p>
    <p>This page shows what an eight-week Eagle Ridge engagement does to that
    number, using a representative eight-person machine shop.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="figtag">Fig. 01 &middot; The scale you are scored on</p>
  <figure>
    <svg data-md-exclude viewBox="0 0 820 92" width="820" height="92" role="img"
         aria-label="Number line from minus 203 to 110 with the 88 conditional-pass threshold marked">
      <line x1="30" y1="46" x2="790" y2="46" stroke="#D9D0BF" stroke-width="2"/>
      <!-- ticks: scale x = 30 + (v+203)/313*760 -->
      <line x1="30" y1="38" x2="30" y2="54" stroke="#9A8E7A" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="30" y="76" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;203</text>
      <text x="30" y="28" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">worst case</text>
      <line x1="790" y1="38" x2="790" y2="54" stroke="#9A8E7A" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="790" y="76" text-anchor="middle" class="num">110</text>
      <text x="790" y="28" text-anchor="end" class="ax">perfect score</text>
      <line x1="736.6" y1="32" x2="736.6" y2="60" stroke="#B14E26" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="736.6" y="76" text-anchor="middle" class="num-t">88</text>
      <circle cx="493.8" cy="46" r="7" fill="#44372F" stroke="#FAF7F0" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="493.8" y="76" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;12</text>
      <text x="493.8" y="28" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">a typical first score</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>The DoD scores all 110 NIST 800-171 controls. Each gap subtracts
    1, 3, or 5 points. Miss every one and you lose 313&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;from 110 all the way
    down to &minus;203.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>One engagement, one number</h2>
    <p>Everything in the engagement moves one number. First we find out where
    you actually stand&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;no sugarcoating, because the assessor won&rsquo;t
    sugarcoat either. Then the rest of the engagement climbs the score back over
    the line, with the few small items left over on a formal remediation plan the
    rule recognizes (a&nbsp;POA&amp;M).</p>
  </div>

  <p class="figtag">Fig. 02 &middot; A representative engagement, start to submission</p>
  <figure>
    <svg data-md-exclude viewBox="0 0 860 420" width="860" height="420" role="img"
         aria-label="Waterfall chart: score starts at 110, gaps reduce it to minus 12, remediation raises it to 91, above the 88 threshold">
      <!-- y(v) = 20 + (115 - v) * 2.345 ; baseline y(0)=289.7 -->
      <!-- threshold 88 -> y 83.3 -->
      <line x1="30" y1="83.3" x2="790" y2="83.3" stroke="#1A1614"
            stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="6 5"/>
      <text x="346" y="75" text-anchor="middle" class="thresh">88 &middot; conditional-pass line</text>
      <!-- zero baseline -->
      <line x1="30" y1="289.7" x2="790" y2="289.7" stroke="#D9D0BF" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="24" y="293" text-anchor="end" class="ax">0</text>

      <!-- 1: start 110  (0..110) -->
      <rect x="40" y="31.7" width="72" height="258" rx="4" fill="#44372F">
        <title>Every contractor starts at 110</title></rect>
      <text x="76" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="num">110</text>
      <text x="76" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">start</text>

      <!-- 2: 5-pt gaps: 110 -> 25 -->
      <rect x="148" y="31.7" width="72" height="199.4" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A">
        <title>17 five-point gaps: MFA, FIPS encryption, logging &#8722;85</title></rect>
      <text x="184" y="24" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;85</text>
      <text x="184" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">5-pt gaps</text>
      <text x="184" y="324" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">MFA, FIPS, logging</text>

      <!-- 3: 3-pt gaps: 25 -> 7 -->
      <rect x="256" y="231.1" width="72" height="42.2" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A">
        <title>6 three-point gaps &#8722;18</title></rect>
      <text x="292" y="224" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;18</text>
      <text x="292" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">3-pt gaps</text>

      <!-- 4: 1-pt gaps: 7 -> -12 -->
      <rect x="364" y="273.3" width="72" height="44.5" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A">
        <title>19 one-point gaps &#8722;19</title></rect>
      <text x="400" y="266" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;19</text>
      <text x="400" y="336" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">1-pt gaps</text>

      <!-- 5: today total -12 (0 down to -12) -->
      <rect x="472" y="289.7" width="72" height="28.1" rx="4" fill="#44372F">
        <title>Score after an honest gap assessment: &#8722;12</title></rect>
      <text x="508" y="334" text-anchor="middle" class="num">&#8722;12</text>
      <text x="508" y="352" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl-b">week 2: the truth</text>

      <!-- 6: remediation rise -12 -> 91 -->
      <rect x="580" y="76.3" width="72" height="241.5" rx="4" fill="#B14E26">
        <title>Remediation (weeks 2&#8211;4) closes the gaps: +103. SSP writing and review then prove the score holds.</title></rect>
      <text x="616" y="68" text-anchor="middle" class="num-t">+103</text>
      <text x="616" y="336" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl">remediation</text>
      <text x="616" y="352" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">weeks 2&ndash;4</text>

      <!-- 7: final 91 -->
      <rect x="688" y="76.3" width="72" height="213.4" rx="4" fill="#44372F">
        <title>Submitted score: 91, with 19 small items on a POA&amp;M</title></rect>
      <text x="724" y="68" text-anchor="middle" class="num">91</text>
      <text x="724" y="308" text-anchor="middle" class="lbl-b">submitted</text>
      <text x="724" y="324" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">19 pts on POA&amp;M</text>

      <!-- connectors -->
      <g stroke="#B9B093" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 3">
        <line x1="112" y1="31.7" x2="148" y2="31.7"/>
        <line x1="220" y1="231.1" x2="256" y2="231.1"/>
        <line x1="328" y1="273.3" x2="364" y2="273.3"/>
        <line x1="436" y1="317.8" x2="472" y2="317.8"/>
        <line x1="544" y1="317.8" x2="580" y2="317.8"/>
        <line x1="652" y1="76.3" x2="688" y2="76.3"/>
      </g>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Representative eight-person shop: seventeen 5-point gaps, six
    3-point, nineteen 1-point. Weights come from the official DoD Assessment
    Methodology; the submitted score keeps 19 points of one-point items on a
    POA&amp;M, under the 22 points the 88 threshold leaves you.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>All 110 controls, accounted for</h2>
    <p>An assessor marks each control met or not met&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;only two controls
    (MFA and FIPS encryption) carry partial credit. We assess all 110 in the
    first two weeks, fix what moves the score, and put the rest on the
    POA&amp;M.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="figtag">Fig. 03 &middot; Where the 110 controls stand</p>
  <figure>
    <svg data-md-exclude viewBox="0 0 860 190" width="860" height="190" role="img"
         aria-label="Two stacked bars: at week 2, 68 of 110 controls met and 42 not met; at week 7, 91 met and 19 one-point items on the POA&amp;M">
      <defs>
        <pattern id="hatchT" width="7" height="7" patternTransform="rotate(45)"
                 patternUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <rect width="7" height="7" fill="#FAF7F0"/>
          <line x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="7" stroke="#B14E26" stroke-width="2.4"/>
        </pattern>
      </defs>
      <!-- 6px per control, x0=150; 2px paper gaps between segments -->
      <text x="140" y="52" text-anchor="end" class="lbl-b">week 2</text>
      <rect x="150" y="30" width="406" height="34" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A">
        <title>68 controls met</title></rect>
      <rect x="558" y="30" width="250" height="34" rx="4" fill="#B14E26">
        <title>42 controls not met</title></rect>
      <text x="353" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="num">68 met</text>
      <text x="683" y="52" text-anchor="middle" class="num" fill="#FAF7F0">42 not met</text>

      <text x="140" y="122" text-anchor="end" class="lbl-b">week 7</text>
      <rect x="150" y="100" width="544" height="34" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A">
        <title>91 controls met</title></rect>
      <rect x="696" y="100" width="112" height="34" rx="4" fill="url(#hatchT)" stroke="#B14E26" stroke-width="1">
        <title>19 one-point items on the POA&amp;M, each with a 180-day deadline</title></rect>
      <text x="422" y="122" text-anchor="middle" class="num">91 met</text>
      <text x="752" y="156" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">19 on POA&amp;M</text>
      <line x1="752" y1="138" x2="752" y2="144" stroke="#B14E26" stroke-width="1.5"/>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Hatched items are open but accepted: a POA&amp;M is the DoD&rsquo;s
    formal way to let you certify now and close the small gaps inside 180 days.
    Close them and the certification goes Final; miss the 180 days and it lapses.
    Most one-point controls qualify, a few are excluded outright, and one
    five-point control qualifies only at partial credit&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;we verify
    eligibility item by item.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Eight weeks, start to assessor</h2>
    <p>The work overlaps on purpose. While you and your IT support close technical
    gaps, we write the System Security Plan&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;the document the assessor
    reads first. Then we review it the way an assessor will, and keep reviewing
    until there are no critical findings left.</p>
  </div>

  <p class="figtag">Fig. 04 &middot; The engagement, week by week</p>
  <figure>
    <svg data-md-exclude viewBox="0 0 860 330" width="860" height="330" role="img"
         aria-label="Timeline of seven engagement phases across eight weeks: discovery week 1; gap assessment week 2; remediation weeks 2 to 4; SSP writing weeks 3 to 5; assessor-style review weeks 5 to 6; evidence and prep weeks 6 to 7; C3PAO assessment week 8 and after">
      <!-- weeks: x = 166 + (w-1)*80, col width 80 -->
      <g class="ax" text-anchor="middle">
        <text x="206" y="20">wk 1</text><text x="286" y="20">wk 2</text>
        <text x="366" y="20">wk 3</text><text x="446" y="20">wk 4</text>
        <text x="526" y="20">wk 5</text><text x="606" y="20">wk 6</text>
        <text x="686" y="20">wk 7</text><text x="766" y="20">wk 8+</text>
      </g>
      <g stroke="#EAE4D4" stroke-width="1">
        <line x1="166" y1="30" x2="166" y2="300"/><line x1="246" y1="30" x2="246" y2="300"/>
        <line x1="326" y1="30" x2="326" y2="300"/><line x1="406" y1="30" x2="406" y2="300"/>
        <line x1="486" y1="30" x2="486" y2="300"/><line x1="566" y1="30" x2="566" y2="300"/>
        <line x1="646" y1="30" x2="646" y2="300"/><line x1="726" y1="30" x2="726" y2="300"/>
        <line x1="806" y1="30" x2="806" y2="300"/>
      </g>
      <!-- rows at y = 38 + i*38, band h 24 -->
      <g class="lbl" text-anchor="end">
        <text x="156" y="55">discovery</text>
        <text x="156" y="93">gap assessment</text>
        <text x="156" y="131">remediation</text>
        <text x="156" y="169">SSP writing</text>
        <text x="156" y="207">assessor-style review</text>
        <text x="156" y="245">evidence &amp; prep</text>
        <text x="156" y="283">C3PAO assessment</text>
      </g>
      <rect x="166" y="38"  width="78"  height="24" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A"><title>Week 1: intake, CUI determination, system boundary</title></rect>
      <rect x="246" y="76"  width="78"  height="24" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A"><title>Week 2: all 110 controls assessed, honest score</title></rect>
      <rect x="246" y="114" width="238" height="24" rx="4" fill="#B14E26"><title>Weeks 2&#8211;4: the score-moving fixes</title></rect>
      <rect x="326" y="152" width="238" height="24" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A"><title>Weeks 3&#8211;5: 110 control narratives</title></rect>
      <rect x="486" y="190" width="158" height="24" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A"><title>Weeks 5&#8211;6: iterate until zero critical findings</title></rect>
      <rect x="566" y="228" width="158" height="24" rx="4" fill="#9A8E7A"><title>Weeks 6&#8211;7: evidence binder, interview prep, score submission</title></rect>
      <rect x="726" y="266" width="78"  height="24" rx="4" fill="none"
            stroke="#B14E26" stroke-width="2" stroke-dasharray="5 4"><title>Week 8+: the certified third-party assessment</title></rect>
      <text x="765" y="316" text-anchor="middle" class="ax">their exam, our prep</text>
    </svg>
    <figcaption>Remediation (weeks 2&ndash;4) is the heaviest lift; the dashed bar at
    the end is the assessment itself, run by an independent certified
    assessor&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;a C3PAO. The seven weeks before it exist to make that week
    boring.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

<section>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Your hours vs. ours</h2>
    <p>You run a shop, not a security team. The engagement keeps your part short
    and specific. We do the document-heavy work.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cols">
    <div class="you">
      <h3>What you do</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Answer the intake questionnaire and one structured call</li>
        <li>Gather the evidence we list&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;screenshots, invoices, settings</li>
        <li>Approve tool purchases and let IT apply the config changes</li>
        <li>Sign policies and sit for a practice interview</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="us">
      <h3>What Eagle Ridge does</h3>
      <ul>
        <li>Assess all 110 controls and score you the way the DoD will</li>
        <li>Prioritize fixes by points-per-dollar for a small-shop budget</li>
        <li>Draft the SSP&rsquo;s 110 control narratives and the POA&amp;M</li>
        <li>Review it assessor-style, package evidence, prep your people</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<p class="note">Figures show a representative engagement, not a quote&thinsp;&mdash;&thinsp;your
starting score and timeline depend on your systems. Scoring follows the DoD
Assessment Methodology; a Registered Provider reviews every deliverable before
it reaches you. The SSP is delivered gap-documented and becomes
assessment-ready once policies are signed and tools are deployed.<br>
Sources: DoD NIST SP 800-171 Assessment Methodology v1.2.1 (2020) &middot; 32 CFR
Part 170 (CMMC Program, &sect;170.21) &middot; NIST SP 800-171 Rev 2.<br>
Eagle Ridge Advisory &middot; <a href="mailto:chris@eagleridge.io">chris@eagleridge.io</a> &middot;
<a href="https://eagleridge.io">eagleridge.io</a></p>

</div>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
